  "solution_html": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 200\"><circle cx=\"100.00\" cy=\"100.00\" r=\"64.00\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" fill=\"none\" /><text x=\"25.00\" y=\"100.00\" fill=\"#0000ff\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" dominant-baseline=\"hanging\">K</text><text x=\"170.00\" y=\"100.00\" fill=\"#0000ff\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" dominant-baseline=\"hanging\">G</text><line x1=\"160.00\" y1=\"96.00\" x2=\"168.00\" y2=\"104.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"160.00\" y1=\"104.00\" x2=\"168.00\" y2=\"96.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><text x=\"100.00\" y=\"80.00\" fill=\"#ff0000\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" dominant-baseline=\"hanging\">D</text><line x1=\"96.00\" y1=\"96.00\" x2=\"104.00\" y2=\"104.00\" stroke=\"#ff0000\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"96.00\" y1=\"104.00\" x2=\"104.00\" y2=\"96.00\" stroke=\"#ff0000\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"32.00\" y1=\"96.00\" x2=\"40.00\" y2=\"104.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"32.00\" y1=\"104.00\" x2=\"40.00\" y2=\"96.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"36.00\" y1=\"100.00\" x2=\"164.00\" y2=\"100.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"64.00\" y1=\"108.00\" x2=\"66.00\" y2=\"92.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"67.00\" y1=\"108.00\" x2=\"69.00\" y2=\"92.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"136.00\" y1=\"92.00\" x2=\"134.00\" y2=\"108.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /><line x1=\"133.00\" y1=\"92.00\" x2=\"131.00\" y2=\"108.00\" stroke=\"#0000ff\" stroke-width=\"1.0\" /></svg>\t<p> <b>On sait que </b>:\tdans le plan muni d'un repère, pour deux points \\(A(x_A;y_A)\\)et \\(B(x_B;y_B)\\) les coordonnées du milieu du segment \\([ A\\,B ]\\) se calculent\tavec la formule suivante :</p>\t<div class=\"wimscenter\">\t(\\(\\frac{x_A+x_B}{2}\\) ; \\(\\frac{y_A+y_B}{2}\\)).\t</div>\t<p>\\(D\\) est le centre du cercle de diamètre \\([ K\\,G ]\\), donc \\(D\\) est le\tmilieu du segment \\([ K\\,G ]\\).</p>\t<p>Les coordonnées \\(\\left(x_{G} ; y_{G}\\right)\\) du point \\(G\\) vérifient donc : </p>\t<div class=\"wimscenter\">\t(\\(\\frac{-3+x_G}{2}\\) ; \\(\\frac{-10+y_G}{2}\\))=(\\(-5\\) ; \\(-1,5\\)).\t</div>\t<p> Il faut résoudre :</p>\t<div class=\"wimscenter\">\t\\(\\frac{-3+x_G}{2}=-5\\) et \\(\\frac{-10+y_G}{2}=-1.5\\).\t</div>\t<p>Ce qui donne :</p>\t<div class=\"wimscenter\">\t\\(x_{G} = -7\\) et \\(y_{G} = 7\\).\t</div>\t"
